{"pass": 1, "id": "GOLD-001", "answerable": true, "gold_doc_paths": ["architecture/nodes.md"], "key_fact_regexes": ["kubelet", "container runtime"], "answer": "The primary components of a Kubernetes worker node are the kubelet, which ensures that Pods are running, and the container runtime, which is responsible for running containers [0]. The kube-proxy (optional) maintains network rules on nodes to implement Services [0]. These components work together to manage and maintain the running Pods on the worker node.", "top_sources": ["architecture/_index.md", "overview/components.md", "overview/_index.md", "resource-management/resource-managers.md", "overview/kubectl.md"], "citations": ["architecture/_index.md", "overview/components.md", "overview/_index.md", "overview/_index.md", "overview/components.md", "architecture/_index.md", "overview/components.md", "overview/_index.md", "overview/_index.md", "overview/components.md"], "answered_by": "qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M", "seconds": 11.7, "attached": [["architecture/_index.md", "overview/components.md", "overview/_index.md", "overview/_index.md", "overview/components.md"]]}
{"pass": 1, "id": "GOLD-002", "answerable": true, "gold_doc_paths": ["architecture/cloud-controller.md"], "key_fact_regexes": ["cloud provider", "control plane"], "answer": "The primary role of the Kubernetes Cloud Controller Manager (CCM) is to manage cloud-specific operations by running controllers that interact with the underlying cloud infrastructure. These controllers include the Node controller, which updates Node objects when new servers are created, and the Service controller, which manages cloud provider load balancers [0]. The CCM enables integration between Kubernetes and various cloud providers through a plugin mechanism [0].", "top_sources": ["architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "overview/components.md", "architecture/controller.md", "security/security-checklist.md"], "citations": ["architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/_index.md"], "answered_by": "qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M", "seconds": 13.6, "attached": [["architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/cloud-controller.md", "architecture/_index.md"]]}
{"pass": 1, "id": "GOLD-003", "answerable": true, "gold_doc_paths": ["architecture/cgroups.md"], "key_fact_regexes": ["cgroup[s]? v2|cgroup2", "unified hierarchy"], "answer": "cgroup v2 provides a single unified hierarchy for resource management in Linux [0]. This unified hierarchy is part of its design improvements over cgroup v1 [0].", "top_sources": ["architecture/cgroups.md", "configuration/windows-resource-management.md", "workloads/workload-api/workloadbuilder.md", "workloads/podgroup-api/_index.md", "cluster-administration/system-metrics.md"], "citations": ["architecture/cgroups.md", "configuration/windows-resource-management.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "configuration/windows-resource-management.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "architecture/cgroups.md"], "answered_by": "qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M", "seconds": 31.8, "attached": [["architecture/cgroups.md", "configuration/windows-resource-management.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "architecture/cgroups.md", "architecture/cgroups.md"]]}
{"pass": 1, "id": "GOLD-004", "answerable": true, "gold_doc_paths": ["architecture/leases.md"], "key_fact_regexes": ["kube-node-lease", "heartbeat"], "answer": "Kubernetes uses Lease objects to communicate kubelet node heartbeats to the API server, with each Node having a corresponding Lease object in the kube-node-lease namespace [0]. Every kubelet heartbeat is an update request to this Lease object, updating the `spec.renewTime` field, which the control plane uses to determine node availability [0].", "top_sources": ["architecture/leases.md", "architecture/nodes.md", "cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election.md", "workloads/pods/pod-lifecycle.md", "overview/working-with-objects/namespaces.md"], "citations": ["architecture/leases.md", "architecture/leases.md", "architecture/nodes.md", "cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election.md", "cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election.md", "architecture/leases.md", "architecture/leases.md", "architecture/nodes.md", "cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election.md", "cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election.md"], "answered_by": "qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M", "seconds": 41.5, "attached": [["architecture/leases.md", "architecture/leases.md", "architecture/nodes.md", "cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election.md", "cluster-administration/coordinated-leader-election.md"]]}
{"pass": 1, "id": "GOLD-005", "answerable": true, "gold_doc_paths": ["architecture/controller.md"], "key_fact_regexes": ["control loop", "desired state"], "answer": "The core design pattern implemented by Kubernetes controllers is to use a control loop that tracks a desired state defined by one kind of resource and manages another kind of resource to achieve that desired state [0]. For example, a Job controller tracks Job objects and creates Pods to run the tasks, thereby managing the cluster state [0]. This pattern allows for modular, independent controllers that can fail without affecting the entire system [0].", "top_sources": ["architecture/controller.md", "overview/components.md", "architecture/_index.md", "extend-kubernetes/operator.md", "extend-kubernetes/api-extension/custom-resources.md"], "citations": ["architecture/controller.md", "overview/components.md", "architecture/controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/controller.md", "architecture/controller.md", "overview/components.md", "architecture/controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/controller.md", "architecture/controller.md", "overview/components.md", "architecture/controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/controller.md"], "answered_by": "qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M", "seconds": 43.2, "attached": [["architecture/controller.md", "overview/components.md", "architecture/controller.md", "architecture/_index.md", "architecture/controller.md"]]}
