{"pass": 1, "id": "GOLD-064", "answerable": true, "gold_doc_paths": ["storage/volume-pvc-datasource.md"], "key_fact_regexes": ["clone", "PersistentVolumeClaim"], "answer": "Cloning a CSI volume creates an exact duplicate of an existing Kubernetes Volume, allowing it to be consumed as any standard Volume. This is achieved by specifying an existing PVC as a dataSource during new PVC creation, where the backend device provisions a copy of the source volume instead of creating a new empty volume [0]. The cloned volume behaves like any other volume but is a duplicate of the original.", "top_sources": ["storage/volume-pvc-datasource.md", "storage/volume-populators-and-data-sources.md", "storage/volumes.md", "storage/volume-snapshots.md", "storage/ephemeral-volumes.md"], "citations": ["storage/volume-pvc-datasource.md", "storage/volume-pvc-datasource.md", "storage/volume-populators-and-data-sources.md", "storage/volumes.md", "storage/volume-snapshots.md"], "answered_by": "qwen3:4b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M", "seconds": 35.8, "attached": [["storage/volume-pvc-datasource.md", "storage/volume-pvc-datasource.md", "storage/volume-populators-and-data-sources.md", "storage/volumes.md", "storage/volume-snapshots.md"]]}
